@page "/docs/troubleshooting/state-between-requests"
@attribute [FollowsModeSwitch]

@* A static page is a new component instance per request: fields start over. Keep state in the
   address ([SupplyParameterFromQuery], links built with GetUriWithQueryParameter) or in posted
   fields. button-state-in-address checked in all three modes. *@

<ArticlePage Section="troubleshooting" Slug="state-between-requests">
    <Lead>
        A static page is built afresh for every request, so a field in the component starts over each time. Keep what the
        page needs in the address, or post it.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Problem</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A value set in one request is gone in the next: a count goes back to its first value, a chosen step resets, a
            list loaded on the first visit is loaded again. Here every post shows 3 guests, however many times it's
            pressed; on an interactive page the same code counts up.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor" Title="Booking.razor" HighlightLines="8">@Broken</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Cause</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            On an interactive page a component instance lives as long as it stays on the page, so its fields keep their values. On
            a static page, each request (a link followed, a form posted, a reload) creates new components, renders them and
            throws them away. Nothing is kept on the server between requests unless you store it.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Fix</Heading>
        <TextBlock>Keep the state where the next request carries it:</TextBlock>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>
                <strong>In the address.</strong> Read it with <Code>[SupplyParameterFromQuery]</Code>, and make each change a
                link that sets it with <Code>NavigationManager.GetUriWithQueryParameter</Code>, which keeps the rest of the
                query string. It survives a reload, and the page can be shared or bookmarked as it is.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <strong>In the form.</strong> Fields post their values, and the page reads them with
                <Code>[SupplyParameterFromForm]</Code>. A value with no field of its own can post in a hidden
                <Code>&lt;input&gt;</Code>.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <strong>Elsewhere.</strong> A database on the server, or a cookie in the browser for a reader's preferences,
                read on each request.
            </ListItem>
        </List>
        <Code Block Language="razor" Title="Booking.razor" HighlightLines="3,9-10,12">@Fixed</Code>
        <ExampleViewer Example="button-state-in-address" ModeSwitch />
        <TextBlock>
            IzzyBlazor's components use the address the same way: <Code>Table</Code>, <Code>Pagination</Code> and
            <Code>FilterForm</Code> keep their state in the query string, <Code>Tabs</Code> with a <Code>QueryKey</Code>
            opens the tab the address names, and a dialog opens from <Code>?dialog=id</Code>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Related</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">Render modes</Anchor>: state on static pages.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/troubleshooting/onclick">OnClick does nothing on a static page</Anchor>: links and posts instead of events.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/table">Table</Anchor>: sorting, filters and pages in the address.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Broken = """
        <form method="post" @formname="guests" @onsubmit="() => _guests++">
            <AntiforgeryToken />
            <Button Submit>Add a guest</Button>
        </form>
        <TextBlock>@_guests guests</TextBlock>

        @code {
            private int _guests = 2;
        }
        """;

    private const string Fixed = """
        @inject NavigationManager Navigation

        <Button Href="@Navigation.GetUriWithQueryParameter("guests", Guests + 1)">
            Add a guest
        </Button>
        <TextBlock>@Guests guests</TextBlock>

        @code {
            [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "guests")]
            private int? GuestsQuery { get; set; }

            private int Guests => GuestsQuery ?? 2;
        }
        """;
}
